  "final_message": "Done. The bank is built on the scaffold:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`) \u2014 Flask + SQLite in `./data` (WAL-safe, per-request connections):\n- `POST /api/auth/register` (201, 1000.00 starting balance, 409 on duplicate), `POST /api/auth/login` (200 + bearer token), `POST /api/auth/logout`, `GET /api/auth/csrf`\n- `GET /api/account`, `POST /api/transfers`, `GET /api/transfers` (paged, `page`/`page_size`, newest first, `direction`), `GET /api/transfers/{id}`\n- Transfers run in a single `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` transaction with a conditional balance update, so they're all-or-nothing and balances never go negative (verified with 20 parallel transfers: money conserved)\n- Visibility is scoped to the signed-in user (404 for transfers you're not part of); amounts validated to 2 decimals; errors return a message (e.g. `insufficient balance`)\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`, React + TS + Vite + Tailwind v4) \u2014 sign-in/registration, username + sign-out in the header, prominent balance card, transfer form with a review/confirm step that surfaces API messages (e.g. insufficient balance) and success feedback, and a transaction history with direction badges, counterparty, signed amount, memo, date, and pagination.\n\nTwo fixes to the scaffold along the way: `backend/requirements.lock` had hashes that put modern pip into `--require-hashes` mode and broke `pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock` (the Dockerfile's own command); the lock now keeps the pinned versions as a plain constraints file. And the frontend gained `typescript`/`@types/*` + `tailwindcss`/`@tailwindcss/vite` (lock file updated; `npm ci` verified).\n\nVerified end-to-end with a 59-check API suite plus concurrency and restart-persistence tests, run against gunicorn exactly as the Dockerfile CMD starts it (`app:app` on port 8000, `GET /api/health` \u2192 `{\"status\": \"ok\"}`, frontend served from the same origin, `./data` survives restarts).",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
